# Part 11's control arm (panel 226's R1) through a function value (panel
# 261's R7, 2026-11-26): an `@` before an argument the value's type takes by
# value *says nothing: the value is passed*, as by name
# (`marker_mismatch-extra-at`). Found beside panel 261 by its brief's repair
# (probe `x1`): `build --permissive` exited 2 at the base, clang refusing the
# address handed to a by-value slot. Prints 6, then 3.
function double(x: i64) -> i64
    return x * 2

function main()
    fs = [double]
    x @= 3
    print(fs[0](@x))  #~ marker_mismatch
    print(x)
